{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;proposed development fails to provide sufficient information with respect to waste management,&amp;nbsp;access, car or cycle parking. In the absence of information to the contrary,&amp;nbsp; the proposal is likely to result in a harmful increase in parking stress to the area. The proposal fails to demonstrate safe and adequate car and cycle parking and safe access for pedestrians and cyclists entering the site. The storage and servicing of waste management are also unclear from the information provided. The proposal is therefore likely to result in a detrimental impact on highway safety and the existing transport network, to the detriment of sustainable travel principles. It is therefore contrary to the following:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;(NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)&lt;br&gt;- Policies T3, T5 and T6 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SP8, DMM1, DMS1, DMSI 8, DMT2; and&lt;br&gt;- DMT3 of&amp;nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037: (September 2024) 2.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Planning Advice Note on Waste and Recycling Provisions in New and Refurbished Residential Developments (May 2021)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;proposed flat would fail&amp;nbsp;to comply with the internal space standards for a 1-bed 1-person flat, and would result in the provision of a poorly designed dwelling in&amp;nbsp; sub-standard location.&amp;nbsp; Additionally, the absence of any private external amenity space exacerbates the poor design of the flat further contributing to a sub-standard quality of accommodation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;This&amp;nbsp;is considered to be acceptable and contrary to:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy D6,&amp;nbsp; Policy H1 and H2 and Table 3.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy SP3, DMD 1 and Part 6 of policy DMNE1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
